            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A sole structure for an article of footwear includes a fluid-filled bladder and a cushioning member. The bladder includes a first segment extending along a medial side of the sole structure, a second segment extending along a lateral side of the sole structure, and a first conduit extending between and fluidly coupling the first segment and the second segment. The cushioning member includes a pocket having a first recess extending along the medial side of the sole structure and receiving the first segment of the fluid-filled bladder, a second recess extending along the lateral side of the sole structure and receiving the second segment of the fluid-filled bladder, and a first channel extending between the first recess and the second recess and receiving the first conduit of the fluid-filled bladder.</p>
            </abstract>
